rule door v1
description "How a door moves on one action: a push strong enough opens it, a bolt locks it, and unbolting it costs a call-out fee. An example written for the purpose of what a file's claims leave open"

enum door_state = closed | open | locked
enum door_action = push | bolt | unbolt

inputs
  state  : door_state
  action : door_action
  force  : number  range >=0 <=10

outputs
  next_state : door_state
  moved      : bool
  fee        : money[USD]  range >=0USD <=5USD  round down(1USD)

table step
policy unique
| state  | action     | force | -> next_state | moved | fee  |
| closed | push       | <5    | state         | false | 0USD |
| closed | push       | >=5   | open          | true  | 0USD |
| closed | bolt       | -     | locked        | true  | 0USD |
| closed | unbolt     | -     | state         | false | 0USD |
| locked | unbolt     | -     | closed        | true  | 2USD |
| locked | push, bolt | -     | state         | false | 0USD |
| open   | -          | -     | state         | false | 0USD |  # an open door stays open: nothing here closes it

machine door over step
  carry   state -> next_state
  initial closed
  final   open
  never   locked after open

# A bolted door has to be unbolted before it can be pushed open.
scenario unbolted_first
| action | force | -> next_state | moved | fee  |
| bolt   | 0     | locked        | true  | 0USD |
| unbolt | 0     | closed        | true  | 2USD |
| push   | 7     | open          | true  | 0USD |

examples
| state  | action | force | -> next_state | moved | fee  |
| closed | push   | 4     | closed        | false | 0USD |
